      "Title": "Open with the world doing its work",
      "Status": "fail",
      "Evidence": "The story opens directly with heist tension already engaged (\u0027The job was going beautifully. That was always when you had to watch it.\u0027) and plunges into active infiltration, drones, and counter-intrusion alarms within the first paragraphs \u2014 there is no grounded commute/transaction beat where a jaded local simply moves through the world before the plot demands attention.",
      "Fix": "Precede the heist with a short, low-stakes beat of the protagonist doing something mundane in her world (paying for something, riding transit, reading a machine\u0027s hum) so the reader falls into the setting before the crisis begins."
    },
    {
