      "Status": "warn",
      "Evidence": "Terms like \u0027neuretics\u0027 (used immediately for embodied action: \u0027Her neuretics ran a direct line into the building\u0027s maintenance scheduler\u0027) and \u0027Husk\u0027 are glossed lightly through function, but \u0027CorpoNations\u0027 and \u0027\u03A6\u0027 currency and \u0027GLMZ\u0027/\u0027The Low\u0027/\u0027Seam margin\u0027 are dropped in with only partial orientation (\u0027GLMZ \u2014 the biggest stretch of gray-zone machinery in the northern hemisphere, ten times Detroit\u0027s machine density\u0027 is a clean gloss, but \u0027CorpoNation-adjacent,\u0027 \u0027CorpoNation registry node,\u0027 and \u0027\u03A6\u0027 amounts appear dozens of times with no first-touch anchoring at all, relying on context alone).",
      "Fix": "Give \u0027CorpoNations\u0027 and the \u03A6 currency one brief in-voice orienting beat at their true first mention (e.g., a passing thought like \u0027a CorpoNation name \u2014 the kind of backing that bought silence from ArcSec\u0027 or noting \u03A6 as \u0027the going gray-zone scrip\u0027 when she first counts it) rather than letting readers infer their meaning purely from repeated exposure."
    },
    {
