      "Title": "Never an acronym before its term",
      "Status": "fail",
      "Evidence": "\u0027GLMZ\u0027 is used repeatedly throughout (e.g., \u0027She\u0027d been planning the move for a year... GLMZ \u2014 the biggest stretch of gray-zone machinery in the northern hemisphere\u0027) without ever giving its full expanded term; similarly \u0027ArcSec\u0027 appears (\u0027A Scalpel crew didn\u0027t live this far outside its own territory... ArcSec didn\u0027t keep that quiet\u0027) with no expansion at first use, and \u0027CorpoNation\u0027 is treated as a known compound term without explanation.",
      "Fix": "Introduce GLMZ (and ArcSec) with an in-voice full-term gloss at first mention, e.g., \u0027the Great Lakes Machine Zone\u2014GLMZ, everyone called it,\u0027 before ever using the bare acronym."
