      "Status": "pass",
      "Evidence": "The boots-and-paper detail (padded every morning, then quietly unpadded without her noticing when it changed) works as a complete emotional beat on first read, but a returning reader who knows the ending \u2014 her choosing \u0027Pixel\u0027 and stepping into a new identity \u2014 will recognize it retroactively as the story\u0027s real thesis stated early and physically: she outgrew the old inheritance without marking the moment. Similarly, the AI-warmth motif (\u0027it seemed glad to have been noticed\u0027) reads as flavor on a first pass but becomes a thematic rhyme with her own choice to let 2D\u0027s door stay closed and to open herself to Kyle, once a reader has the whole arc.",
